WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.900
Which names does a GCC tenant use?

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.050
Getting this wrong fails quietly.

3
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:10.261
A GCC tenant keeps using the worldwide
Graph and sign-in endpoints, and Microsoft

4
00:00:10.261 --> 00:00:15.550
says access tokens from one national cloud
aren't interchangeable with another's.

5
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.412
The provisioning agent has
its own list of relay names,

6
00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:22.587
the public cloud's, which
GCC tenants also use.

7
00:00:22.587 --> 00:00:26.101
It needs no inbound ports,
and Microsoft's guidance,

8
00:00:26.101 --> 00:00:30.787
from search excerpts, is to avoid
inline TLS inspection on that path.

9
00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:35.172
The practical lesson is simple: keep
a list of the names your tenant uses,

10
00:00:35.172 --> 00:00:37.476
and test through the real egress path.

11
00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:40.080
Now to Oracle, and a common mistake.
